        {
          "id": 2554531563,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "wimaxasncp/dictionary.xml doesn't have entities (at least in the files that Wireshark provides), but diameter does (and will require the XML_PARSE_NOENT).  In some sense this patch was a \"second data point\" for the work on diameter XML files.  When reading about the option, it seemed to come down to how much \"control\" we have over the dictionary files and I'm not sure how to answer that since it's designed to have \"vendor specific/outside\" files (but I presume we trust the files we distribute)",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
