        {
          "id": 2558861523,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Me not understanding the definition of \"external content\".  My understanding was that entities are like a #include in C and it's a way to properly encapsulate data. And that adding XML_PARSE_NO_XXE would mean those #includes wouldn't be added/parsed, even if they were local XML files (because they are \"external\" to the XML document currently being parsed).  And that seemed bad.\n\nI also don't understand why \"parsing XML\" presents a security concern (presuming all string parsing is done correctly).  Are the entities \"forcing\" a download of linked files, in which case they could be malicious?  How I read the documentation was that the \"supporting XML\" (again more for diameter for our needs) wouldn't be loaded.",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
