        {
          "id": 2558948917,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "Do we pass the burden onto the user with a preference to use XML_PARSE_NO_XXE?  If we add XML_PARSE_NO_XXE by default, I think we break backwards compatibility of the diameter behavior because the \"supporting\" XML files wouldn't be read (unsure about WiMax because Wireshark doesn't provide any entity files for it, but the previous parser did handle the functionality).",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
