        {
          "id": 2650998592,
          "type": "DiffNote",
          "body": "I think at minimum we should add XML_PARSE_NONET so that it will not attempt to use the built-in HTTP or FTP clients (which were removed in 2.15.0). And I think it's probably worth adding XML_PARSER_NO_XXE (at least for versions of libxml2 that support the option) to the protocol parsing like WiMax that can handle it (and which never supported including external DTDs or entities in the hand-rolled implementation), and think about Diameter later.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
